.TH "PB-ENV-TEAM-ROTATE" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-env-team-rotate - Rotate an encrypted ENV team key while preserving its values


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb env team rotate <team> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Rotate an encrypted ENV team key while preserving its values

.PP
Replace the team scope key while preserving its values for remaining authorized members. The command requires an exact confirmation for this custody transition.

.PP
Team ENV scopes have their own encrypted keys and explicit account grants. Rotation preserves values while replacing access keys; reset discards values. Review the confirmation and affected members before changing custody.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--confirm\fP=""
	exact confirmation phrase: ROTATE ENV TEAM <team>

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for rotate

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-env-team(1)\fP
